    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "Comparing the three models in this atlas",
      "text": "Wan modulates every block by the timestep and cross-attends text. H3 puts every modality in one sequence and looks modulation up per row. Gemma has no conditioning at all — it varies the LAYERS instead, alternating two attention geometries, and brackets each sublayer in four norms.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "definition",
          "src": "gemma4.hf",
